+## Executive decision
+
+Accepted 16f is a strong local success and a weak global signal. It proves that a carefully typed source arrow plus a complete polynomial reference plus local simple/double consumers can retire an actual degree pair; it does not make F9 representative of all configurations below 140. Accepted 16e moves the conditional source-level floor to maximum degree at least 125, but the unresolved 126/128/132/135 configurations and the lack of a cofinal type/degree theorem prevent a new maximum-140 story.
+
+My highest-value proof direction is therefore a **contact-divisor budget** extracted from the F9 proof: turn line-by-line local consumers into a reusable divisor-capacity inequality before choosing another finite source. The strongest orthogonal direction is a **marked-sheet transfer obstruction for a cubic non-Galois block**, using the `A^2` first leg that BD-GAL says any successor must use. These are mechanisms, not promoted theorems.
+
+The counterexample side has no launch-ready complete source ideal. Every recently complete finite ideal named in the packet is now existentially a unit or otherwise retired at its exact scope. The characteristic-109/Witt--`A_infinity` route remains the only constructive disproof mechanism with an actual surviving tower, but this packet does not contain its exact current state; it should be redesigned around a frozen polar-valuation interface before further computation. A necessary receiver, modular survivor, formal germ, or timeout is not a counterexample.
